Independent adversarial review. A separate reviewer agent rebuilt the stubs from the JSON and re-proved the assembly. It also re-checked:
- coercions and statement truth;
- edge cases P = 0, m = 0, x = 0, R < 0, non-integrable integrands and ‖x‖ = s;
- name collisions;
- schema validity.
Verdict: ACCEPT, no blocking defects. Its two minor points were applied:
- The new names use the prefix iwl_cr_cest_* rather than iwl_cr_ce_*, which the sibling cone_exists decomposition already uses (e.g. iwl_cr_ce_cutoff_radial_operator).
- The reuse records are copied verbatim.

Names. The 4 new names collide with none of the 458 dag.json lean_names, no subproblem name in any nodes/*/decomposition-v*.json, and no substring in the 4,916 nodes/*/*.json files. The 2 reused names are `accepted` with byte-identical frozen types.
